font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course adopts an integrated teaching approach combining lectures, case analysis, and group discussion to systematically introduce the basic concepts, theoretical foundations, analytical frameworks, and implementation pathways of value-based healthcare. The course covers key topics including patient outcomes and experience, value measurement, payment mechanisms, resource allocation, service delivery redesign, low-value care reduction, data analytics, and digital health applications. It also draws on international frontier developments and China’s healthcare reform practices to examine the application scenarios and development trends of value-based healthcare in hospital management, healthcare service improvement, and health policy. Through this course, students are expected to enhance their understanding and recognition of the concepts and methods of value-based healthcare, and to strengthen their ability to analyze real-world problems and propose improvement strategies using value-oriented thinking.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
